@startuml
!theme plain
autonumber
title Figure 4 - Spec-Driven Development (Detailed Workflow)

participant "Product Owner" as PO
participant "Architect" as AR
participant "Developer" as DEV
participant "AI\n(Discover role)" as AID
participant "AI\n(Design role)" as AIH
participant "AI\n(Task role)" as AIT
participant "Implementation\nAgents" as IA
database "Product Backlog" as BL

== Discover Phase (What / Why) ==
PO -> BL: Select prioritized feature
loop Iterative intent articulation
  PO -> AID: Share business context and outcomes
  AID --> PO: Clarify assumptions and draft discover spec
  PO -> PO: Refine requirements and acceptance criteria
end
PO -> AR: Handoff Discover spec

== Design Phase (How) ==
loop Technical alignment
  AR -> AIH: Map discover spec to architecture
  AIH --> AR: Propose modules, interfaces, constraints
  AR -> PO: Review trade-offs and architecture fit
  PO --> AR: Confirm or adjust intent
end
AR -> DEV: Handoff Design spec

== Task Phase (Execution Plan) ==
loop Task shaping
  DEV -> AIT: Convert design into executable tasks
  AIT --> DEV: Tasks with checks and parallelization options
  DEV -> DEV: Finalize verifiable task plan
end
DEV -> IA: Dispatch tasks for autonomous execution

== Execution and Review ==
loop Until implementation aligns with specs
  IA -> IA: Implement tasks in parallel
  IA --> DEV: Return code/results
  DEV -> DEV: Validate against discover/design/task specs
  DEV -> AIT: Request targeted fixes for gaps
end
DEV -> BL: Mark work done and update status
DEV -> PO: Share outcome and capture feedback

@enduml
